{"path":"experimental/ranges/algorithm/adjacent_find","title":"std::experimental::ranges::adjacent_find","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::</span>adjacent_find","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/algorithm/adjacent_find","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Notwithstanding the declarations depicted above, the actual number and order of template parameters for algorithm declarations is unspecified.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/ranges/algorithm\">&lt;experimental/ranges/algorithm&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> ForwardIterator I, Sentinel<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>I<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> S, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Proj <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/identity\"><span class=\"kw2857\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">identity</span></span></a>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; IndirectRelation<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/iterator/projected\"><span class=\"kw2695\">projected</span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>I, Proj<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> Pred <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/equal_to\"><span class=\"kw2859\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">equal_to</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>I adjacent_find<span class=\"br0\">(</span> I first, S last, Pred pred <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> Pred<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, Proj proj <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> Proj<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> ForwardRange R, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Proj <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/identity\"><span class=\"kw2857\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">identity</span></span></a>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; IndirectRelation<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/iterator/projected\"><span class=\"kw2695\">projected</span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>, Proj<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> Pred <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/equal_to\"><span class=\"kw2859\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">equal_to</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/iterator/dangling\"><span class=\"kw2872\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">safe_iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>R<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> adjacent_find<span class=\"br0\">(</span> R<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> r, Pred pred <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> Pred<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, Proj proj <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> Proj<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Searches the range <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">first</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">last</span></code><code>)</code></span> for two consecutive identical elements. Elements are compared using <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pred</span></code> after being projected with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">proj</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Same as <span class=\"t-v\">(1)</span>, but uses <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">r</span></code> as the source range, as if using <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">first</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/end\"><span class=\"kw2902\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">end</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>r<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">last</span></code>.</div>\n<p>Notwithstanding the declarations depicted above, the actual number and order of template parameters for algorithm declarations is unspecified. Thus, if explicit template arguments are used when calling an algorithm, the program is probably non-portable.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> first, last\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the range of elements to examine\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> r\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the range of elements to examine\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> pred\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> predicate to use to compare the projected elements\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> proj\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> projection to apply to the elements\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>An iterator to the first of the first pair of identical elements, that is, the first iterator <code>i</code> such that both <code>i</code> and <code>i + 1</code> are in the range <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">first</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">last</span></code><code>)</code></span> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/invoke\"><span class=\"kw2858\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">invoke</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pred, <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/invoke\"><span class=\"kw2858\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">invoke</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>proj, <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/invoke\"><span class=\"kw2858\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">invoke</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>proj, <span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>If no such elements are found, an iterator that compares equal to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">last</span></code> is returned.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>If the range is nonempty, exactly <code>min((result - first) + 1, (last - first) - 1)</code> applications of the predicate where <code>result</code> is the return value, and at most twice as many applications of the projection.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<table class=\"eq-fun-cpp-table\">\n<tr>\n<td>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>ForwardIterator I, Sentinel<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>I<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> S, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Proj <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/identity\"><span class=\"kw2857\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">identity</span></span></a>,\n         IndirectRelation<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/iterator/projected\"><span class=\"kw2695\">projected</span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>I, Proj<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> Pred <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/equal_to\"><span class=\"kw2859\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">equal_to</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;&gt;</span>\nI adjacent_find<span class=\"br0\">(</span>I first, S last, Pred pred <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> Pred<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, Proj proj <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> Proj<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>first <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> last<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> first<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    I next <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> first<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>next<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">while</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>next <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> last<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/invoke\"><span class=\"kw2858\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">invoke</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>pred, <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/invoke\"><span class=\"kw2858\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">invoke</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>proj, <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>first<span class=\"br0\">)</span>,\n                                 <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/functional/invoke\"><span class=\"kw2858\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">invoke</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>proj, <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>next<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n            <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> first<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>next<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>first<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> next<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/adjacent_find\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>adjacent_find</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  finds the first two adjacent items that are equal (or satisfy a given predicate) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>unique</span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  removes consecutive duplicate elements in a range <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/ranges","title":"Extensions for ranges"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::adjacent_find","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Searches the range [first, last) for two consecutive identical elements."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"first, last, r, pred, proj"},{"label":"Return value","note":"An iterator to the first of the first pair of identical elements, that is, the first iterator i such that both i and i + 1 are in the range [first, last) and…"},{"label":"Complexity","note":"If the range is nonempty, exactly min((result - first) + 1, (last - first) - 1) applications of the predicate where result is the return value, and at most…"},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"adjacent_find","note":"finds the first two adjacent items that are equal (or satisfy a given predicate)"},{"label":"unique","note":"removes consecutive duplicate elements in a range"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":367,"codeBlockCount":1}
